\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Limitations}
\date{2026-11-04}


\p{Here we describe the limitations of the content developed so far, compared against the
full goal set out in the opening prose and the Motivation and aim section above. Read it with a grain
of salt: these limitations need further polishing, and some will be addressed by
developing the notes further.}

\p{No moduli map controls a continuum limit, and none is constructed here.
\ref{fdip-003X} asks for one, and its absence leaves every parameter of a
continuum theory free: nothing relates two backgrounds by a continuum
comparison, so no statement here fixes such a parameter.}

\p{The backgrounds form a groupoid that carries no site, stack or descent. A
local-to-global statement about background objects would need a coverage on the
groupoid, sheaves of morphisms over it and effective descent, which
\ref{fdip-004Q} states with its source; \ref{fdip-0069} proves a finite
local-to-global theorem for laws and notes that it gives no descent data for the
objects and arrows of the background groupoid.}

\p{Whether the finite laws converge to a field theory is asked and not
answered. The comparison on a supplied circle of \ref{fdip-004J} controls one
fixed Fourier mode, which is not a continuum limit of the full induced law.
\ref{fdip-003X} states what a physical interpretation would require, and
[Discrete induction and its open interfaces](fdip-003W) records which
comparisons remain open.}

\p{No statement in these notes fixes a spacetime, a physical parameter, a Standard
Model equation or a gravitational equation.}
